Story: Taking a tower
  As a commander of a team
  I want to know how long my drones need at a tower
  So that I send enough drones, and not too many

  You send drones to circle the west tower, and you watch its control bar. One drone takes the
  tower in 20 s. Two drones take it in 10 s. A drone that lands next to the tower does not help.

  Scenario: One drone gets half way in 10 seconds
    Given the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is 50 %
    And the west tower is neutral

  Scenario: One drone takes the tower in 20 seconds
    Given the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 20 seconds
    Then the west tower is held by Blue
    And the control of the west tower is 100 %

  Scenario: Two drones take the tower in 10 seconds
    Given the Blue drones in the west circle are 2
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the west tower is held by Blue

  Scenario: A drone on the ground does not help
    Given the Blue drones on the ground in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is 0 %

Story: Fighting for a tower
  As a commander of a team
  I want to know what happens when both teams are at a tower
  So that I know when to send more drones

  Drones of the two teams meet at the west tower. The control bar moves only for the team with
  more drones. When nobody is at the tower, the bar stays where it is. A team keeps its tower
  until the bar gets back to the middle.

  Scenario: Equal teams stop the bar
    Given the control of the west tower is 50 %
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is 50 %
    And the circle of the west tower is contested

  Scenario: The bigger team moves the bar
    Given the Blue drones in the west circle are 2
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is 50 %
    And the circle of the west tower is contested

  Scenario: An empty circle keeps the bar
    Given the control of the west tower is 50 %
    When the game runs for 1 minute
    Then the control of the west tower is 50 %
    And the circle of the west tower is quiet

  Scenario: Red keeps the tower while the bar is on its side
    Given the west tower is held by Red
    And the control of the west tower is -100 %
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is -50 %
    And the west tower is held by Red

  Scenario: Red loses the tower when the bar gets to the middle
    Given the west tower is held by Red
    And the control of the west tower is -50 %
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the west tower is neutral
    And the control of the west tower is 0 %

Story: Winning a game
  As a commander of a team
  I want to know how a game ends
  So that I know when to hold and when to attack

  Each tower gives its team one point each second. The first team to 500 points wins. If the
  clock gets to 0 first, the team with more points wins.

  Scenario: Two towers give two points each second
    Given the towers held by Blue are 2
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the score of Blue is 20 points

  Scenario: Blue gets to 500 points
    Given the score of Blue is 495 points
    And the score of Red is 300 points
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the game of Towers is won by Blue
    And the score of Blue is 500 points

  Scenario: Red has more points at the end of the clock
    Given the time left is 5 s
    And the score of Blue is 200 points
    And the score of Red is 300 points
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the game of Towers is won by Red
    And the time left is 0 s

  Scenario: Equal points at the end of the clock
    Given the time left is 5 s
    And the score of Blue is 300 points
    And the score of Red is 300 points
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the game of Towers is a draw

  Scenario: After the end, nothing changes
    Given the game of Towers is won by Blue
    And the score of Blue is 500 points
    And the score of Red is 300 points
    When the game runs for 1 minute
    Then the score of Blue is 500 points
    And the score of Red is 300 points

Story: Scouting in the fog
  As a commander of a team
  I want to know what my map shows me
  So that I do not trust what I cannot see

  A Red scout flies across the field. Your map shows it while your drones or your towers see
  it. When it goes into the fog, your map keeps the place where you last saw it. A tower in the
  fog can change sides, and your map does not show it until you look again.

  Scenario: A drone sees the scout
    Given the Red scout is near a Blue drone
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is seen

  Scenario: A tower sees the scout
    Given the Red scout is near the Blue home tower
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is seen

  Scenario: The scout in the fog
    Given the Red scout is far from anything Blue
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is unknown

  Scenario: The scout goes into the fog
    Given the Red scout is near a Blue drone
    When the Red scout flies into the fog for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is last seen
    And the age of the Red scout on the Blue map is 10 s

  Scenario: Red takes a tower in the fog
    Given the control of the east tower is -90 %
    And the Red drones in the east circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the east tower is held by Red
    And the east tower on the Blue map is neutral
    When a Blue drone flies near the east tower
    Then the east tower on the Blue map is held by Red

Story: The computer commander
  As a commander of a team
  I want to know what the computer does with its drones
  So that I can play against it

  The computer commander spreads its drones over the towers that it does not hold. When it sees
  an enemy drone near one of its towers, it sends a drone back to defend it. A drone that is
  behind in a fight for a tower goes somewhere else.

  Scenario: The first orders
    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    And the order of the second Blue drone is take the centre tower
    And the order of the third Blue drone is take the east tower

  Scenario: Defending the home tower
    Given the Red scout is near the Blue home tower
    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the second Blue drone is take the Blue home tower

  Scenario: Giving up a lost fight
    Given the control of the west tower is -20 %
    And the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 1
    When the computer commander of Blue plays for 15 seconds
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the Red home tower
